{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502577-opinions-thread-astral-consilium","id":1502577,"title":"Opinions Thread: Astral Consilium","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-08T20:20:54-08:00","id":1502577,"title":"Opinions Thread: Astral Consilium","content":"What assumptions would you make about a Consilium who conducts all of their official buisness -or at least, as much as is feasible- in the Astral? That is, weekly/monthly/periodic Consilium and Caucus meetings held in a relevant Tenemos realm -or a member's Onieros, depending- with no physical meetups unless absolutely necessary. This includes things like mentorship - new apprentices being given means to enter the Astral and trained in their own Onieros whenever possible.<br /> <br /> Spoilering my personal assumptions. Please post your own first, if possible, so we can see similarities and differences!<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Hallows and Demesnes are common, and possibly so are Synesi<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Mind magic is very common - <u>Create Synesi</u> is taught to all Masters.</li> </ol></li> <li>Merits like Astral Adept and Shadow Self are common</li> <li>Imbued Items that affect sleep -bestowing the Astral Adept Merit, casting <u>Dream Reaching</u>, etc- are very common</li> <li>Local Legacies tend towards Astral traditions, such as the Dreamspeakers, Clavicularius\u200b, Bene Ashmodai, Imagineers, etc.</li> <li>Some combination of paranoia and actual physical danger encourage low-contact<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Seer/Banisher/Other Splat dominance of the local?</li> <li>Habits ingrained from a time when Seer/Banisher/Other Splat dominated the local?</li> <li>Alternatively, everyone is too spread out to engage in-person in a reasonable timeframe.</li> </ol></li> <li>A more widespread aversion to and distain for Paradox than normal, since Paradox is easier to surpress in the Astral.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Lower opinions towards Sleepers, since Sleepers are a big reason the Astral is so much safer for magic?</li> <li>Alternatively, higher instances of Paradox, since the Astral's lower risk conditions Mages to be more reckless in the waking world?</li> </ol></li> <li>Heralds are relied on to service Mages who can't reach the Astral for whatever reason, giving the post a lot of influence<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Mages who can't enter the Astral get significantly less say in local politics</li> <li>Cabals with insufficient means for all their members elect a primary representative?</li> </ol></li> <li>Few Mages know each other in person - most have only ever seen the rest in their Dream Forms.</li> <li>Space Magic is out of favor as a communications medium<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Paranoia make Sympathy-Shielding too common for remote contact via <u>Scrying</u>?</li> <li>The Astral is easier to use, since it relies less on knowledge of Arcana to facilitate remote contact?</li> <li>A local Mystery futzes with Space, like in a couple of the Dark Eras settings?</li> </ol></li> </ol></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 02-08-2023, 11:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T20:59:04-08:00","id":1502582,"title":"","content":"Business as usual, pretty much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T21:11:49-08:00","id":1502583,"title":"","content":"Wouldn\u2019t something like this have it\u2019s own Tenemos realm just by being a organization?<br /> <br /> From what I remember of the Sundered World, this actually was a canon practice. It was impractical to travel, and you might be the only Mage in your village, so Mages would communicate through the astral. <br /> <br /> I can see a larger acceptance of unwise behaviors, due to the safety net afforded by the astral. People would act slightly different, kinda like how people act on the internet. The counter point to this is that one can probably spot the unwise, due to how one\u2019s astral appearance works.<br /> <br /> Superficial Looks would be even more influential on social stuff, since in the astral they actually tell you something about people\u2019s conception of themselves. <br /> <br /> People would be more relaxed about going into someone\u2019s Oneiros. Most people really wouldn\u2019t show the inside of their heart to others, with some exceptions. Partially because it\u2019s embarrassing, and partially because it can be used against you and the consequences are really bad if someone does so. I think the pool of people allowed inside *might* be expanded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T21:49:10-08:00","id":1502586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502577-opinions-thread-astral-consilium?p=1502583#post1502583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn\u2019t something like this have it\u2019s own Tenemos realm just by being a organization?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably. I'd imagine that would be the primary assembly-area for normal Consilium buisness, with Caucus -or Order- Relams being used for Caucus functions. That being said, it makes them predictably easy to find.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502577-opinions-thread-astral-consilium?p=1502583#post1502583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I remember of the Sundered World, this actually was a canon practice. It was impractical to travel, and you might be the only Mage in your village, so Mages would communicate through the astral.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, good point! I forgot about that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502577-opinions-thread-astral-consilium?p=1502583#post1502583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Superficial Looks would be even more influential on social stuff, since in the astral they actually tell you something about people\u2019s conception of themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point, that could have a pretty big impact on behaviors among the local Mages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502577-opinions-thread-astral-consilium?p=1502583#post1502583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People would be more relaxed about going into someone\u2019s Oneiros. Most people really wouldn\u2019t show the inside of their heart to others, with some exceptions. Partially because it\u2019s embarrassing, and partially because it can be used against you and the consequences are really bad if someone does so. I think the pool of people allowed inside *might* be expanded.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I'm a bit confused. Doesn't the first sentence kinda contradict the rest? Seems like they'd be acutely more aware of how much damage visitors in their Onieros could do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T22:06:12-08:00","id":1502588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502577-opinions-thread-astral-consilium?p=1502586#post1502586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I'm a bit confused. Doesn't the first sentence kinda contradict the rest? Seems like they'd be acutely more aware of how much damage visitors in their Onieros could do.</div> </div> </div> </div> Maybe. I was trying to explain my conception of normal Mages, and kinda forgot to back up my argument but uh\u2026People get careless when it\u2019s stuff they interact with every day. I\u2019ve been in way too many car accidents, and usually it came around because people were being reckless and being unsafe. Everyone knew the risks, they just decided to ignore them for convenience. If it\u2019s easier to meet in the Oneiros, people very well might. The more you open up to people, the easier it gets. Sometimes too easy for your own good.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T03:37:31-08:00","id":1502597,"title":"","content":"It would be kind of like conducting all your business online, except you\u2019re using magical means to enhance the experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T07:18:04-08:00","id":1502603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502577-opinions-thread-astral-consilium?p=1502597#post1502597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be kind of like conducting all your business online, except you\u2019re using magical means to enhance the experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>No kidding, the concept is shockingly similar. I wonder what that says about the internet that it parallels the collective unconscious. <br /> <br /> I\u2019m kinda reminded of what one of webcomics I read did to depict internet chat rooms, because they author thought it was boring to only draw text. Basically, they drew the characters avatars having the conversation. They then drew when the characters were using the chat to roleplaying a mixed Pok\u00e9mon Star Trek universe, because why not. Depending on where the meetings take place, similar moments could occur.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d like to think several behaviors that people display on the internet would be lessened. Hopefully, people would be less rude to each other, since they can see the other person, you know, as a person, and since it still feels like there would be consequences for their actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T07:58:23-08:00","id":1502604,"title":"","content":"Such a scenario would probably make people like the Herald, Sentinel, Provost and Suspector a lot more prestigious, since they are able to help you locate and communicate with other mages quickly, at least without violating the Precept of Protectorate. Its reasonable for mages to have public routes for traversing their Sanctum's area (with ones with high Sleeper activity being expected to be far less restrictive) and for leaving a message, but that lacks immediacy.<br /> <br /> I could also see that any major topics on top of mind could be debated in their Temenoic Realm, since it would allow greater clarity on how the issue is perceived.<br /> <br /> Flavor wise, I can't help but imagine Cryptopolies utilizing affordable sessions with (imbued) sensory deprivation tanks to allow prospects to become more used to the Astral landcape, all hidden in plain sight as the hallucinations common to the experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-09-2023, 12:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T13:24:41-08:00","id":1502634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502577-opinions-thread-astral-consilium?p=1502604#post1502604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could also see that any major topics on top of mind could be debated in their Temenoic Realm, since it would allow greater clarity on how the issue is perceived.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hadn't considered that! Now, how would it mesh with the Duel Arcane, I wonder, for the really heated debates?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T13:35:50-08:00","id":1502636,"title":"","content":"I should note the Astral has been used for organizational and directive purposes since mages have been maging it up, as demonstrated by the Vinca. It does rely on Demenses, but otherwise, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T14:53:34-08:00","id":1502645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502577-opinions-thread-astral-consilium?p=1502634#post1502634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hadn't considered that! Now, how would it mesh with the Duel Arcane, I wonder, for the really heated debates?</div> </div> </div> </div>When one plays <a href=\"https://youtu.be/iZOwaeAEIw0\" target=\"_blank\">the oldest game</a>, in a world where there are so many supernatural secrets, it really shows how broad your gnostic understanding is.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, winning might not always be desired, because you may lose a philosophical point.<br /> <br /> Dream's opponent concedes after the last item, because as he puts it &quot;What power would hell have if those imprisoned were not able to dream of heaven?&quot;. Sure, they probably could think of something that undoes hope, but that would itself demonstrate their rebellion against heaven is doomed to fail. Its a no win scenario, so its better to take the smaller loss of just the steaks of the duel. Its a fascinating level of nuance inherent to this Astral focused variant of the Duel Arcane.<br /> <br /> <b>Observation: </b>I imagine masters warn students to NEVER agree to one of these against a Fang of Mara or Clavicularius, its not worth the trauma.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T07:42:19-08:00","id":1502747,"title":"","content":"Assuming mages meet up for Consiliium meetings in the Astral. What sort of defenses would they have to make sure things they don't want to attend don't show up?<br /> <br /> If I remember correctly, Space magic works pretty much normally in the astral, so bans could work, with fate exceptions to only allow those who have sworn an oath to the consilium past. They could probably Quarantine a part of the astral too. Mind could force/create Goetia that shows people the way into the area, and guard against things getting in. Since movement inside the astral is wooly at best i imagine it'd require something like this to stop bad people gaining access...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T13:32:33-08:00","id":1502768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502577-opinions-thread-astral-consilium?p=1502747#post1502747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming mages meet up for Consiliium meetings in the Astral. What sort of defenses would they have to make sure things they don't want to attend don't show up?<br /> <br /> If I remember correctly, Space magic works pretty much normally in the astral, so bans could work, with fate exceptions to only allow those who have sworn an oath to the consilium past. They could probably Quarantine a part of the astral too. Mind could force/create Goetia that shows people the way into the area, and guard against things getting in. Since movement inside the astral is wooly at best i imagine it'd require something like this to stop bad people gaining access...</div> </div> </div> </div>It also probably depends on what realm they meet in. Most realms aren't <i>too</i> hostile towards general visitation, but;<br /> <br /> 1. &quot;Realm of [Relevant Caucus/Consilium]&quot; would probably be inherently hostile to acknowledged enemies<br /> <br /> 2. &quot;Realm of Secret, Secure Meetings&quot; I could see being inherently conducive to such gatherings. It would probably count as an Environmental Yantra for any defensive spells set up, like <u>Ban</u> or <u>Ward</u><br /> <br /> 3. An Onieros can be front-loaded with a fuckton on spells, and is going to be VERY hostile towards acknowledged enemies. Also not going to get a lot of wanderers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T16:09:37-08:00","id":1502785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502577-opinions-thread-astral-consilium?p=1502747#post1502747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming mages meet up for Consiliium meetings in the Astral. What sort of defenses would they have to make sure things they don't want to attend don't show up?<br /> <br /> If I remember correctly, Space magic works pretty much normally in the astral, so bans could work, with fate exceptions to only allow those who have sworn an oath to the consilium past. They could probably Quarantine a part of the astral too. Mind could force/create Goetia that shows people the way into the area, and guard against things getting in. Since movement inside the astral is wooly at best I imagine it'd require something like this to stop bad people gaining access...</div> </div> </div> </div>The top 3 ones I imagine:<br /> <br /> 1- Make sure to check the true form of anyone attending, because a masking of Mind can probably falsify the thought form, meaning you now have to worry about the Architects of the Future AND Princes of Many Masks infiltrating.<br /> <br /> 2- Create a Pomerium type of parameter, so long as you have no ill intentions against the Consilium, you can enter and get the informed condition. Break faith with this oath will cause your intent will be revealed and become Beaten Down. Essentially a specialized <i>Sworn Oath</i>.<br /> <br /> 3- If the issue is potentially a charged topic, cast <i>Display of Power</i> to make sure to direct hostilities towards a Duel Arcane, and undermine any potential magical subterfuge.<br /> <br /> Since Astral realms are infinite, patrolling is not that easy, with ideas and topics acting as waypoints for navigation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-11-2023, 10:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T16:24:22-08:00","id":1502788,"title":"","content":"My post got edit-flagged, but the biggest factor I can think of is that an Onieros can be front-loaded with a fuckton of spells. Meetings hosted in one -which has a whole other set of social and political wrangling attached to it- could be made into a pretty formidable bastion","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T19:37:42-08:00","id":1502806,"title":"","content":"I think an Oneiros would be a terrifying place to host a meeting. The host does not risk Paradox for spells cast within, however, its still the seat of their consciousness. Their thoughts, feelings and traumas are laid bare for anyone who knows how to search and doing substantial mental damage is a very real risk.<br /> <br /> While I see a society more focused on the Astral ecosystem being more liberal with granting access, its still a very personal space.<br /> <br /> However, a master of Mind could also shore up their mental defenses to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1475721#post1475721\">create a very well protected space.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-11-2023, 10:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T21:02:00-08:00","id":1502809,"title":"","content":"Agreed. &quot;Hosting&quot; duty probably wouldn't be particularly desirable.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, it could be a dominance display - &quot;I'm so confident in my position that I'll not balk at having others in my mind&quot;.<br /> <br /> On the gripping hand, a mind version of <u>Pocket Dimension</u> to create a partitioned meeting hall within an Onieros seems like something very doable for a Master.<br /> <br /> Edit: imagine your inner demons being ushers for the rest of the Consilium. &quot;Yes, right this way Epopt. Lust will escort you to your box seats. Ah! Heirophant! Irritation-At-Small-Talk will get you situated - he's prepared those canap\u00e9s you like.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 02-12-2023, 12:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-24T06:46:33-07:00","id":1516006,"title":"","content":"As usual, you all are way ahead of me. Any further thoughts on this? I'm making a Sublime Athenaeum caucus for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26736_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26736\" data-vbnamecard=\"26736\">TempleBuilder</a> 's Prospector for our Summer Chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T13:19:27-07:00","id":1516127,"title":"","content":"It wasn\u2019t standard practice, but I did once have my Los Angeles Consilium/Assembly hold Convocation inside the Oneiros of a local fourth-degree master named the Sandcastle King. Astral landscaping was basically his thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T14:10:11-07:00","id":1516255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502577-opinions-thread-astral-consilium?p=1502806#post1502806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their thoughts, feelings and traumas are laid bare for anyone who knows how to search and doing substantial mental damage is a very real risk.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems to me that mages are technically at risk any time they decide to meet in numbers, at least assuming they have great reason to assume that their fellows are hostile and won't respect the rules.<br /> <br /> If you invite somebody into your Oneiros and they overstep their bounds, society can punish them.<br /> <br /> And they presumably have to be motivated to do so, unless one is going for a presentation of &quot;nobody trusts or respects one another and they're all constantly going for the throat&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}